{#
    The shell every HTML email in this application extends.

    Email is not the web, and three constraints in particular shape what is below:

      1. **Every style is inline.** No CSS inliner is installed (`twig/cssinliner-extra` is not a
         dependency) and several clients strip a `<style>` element outright, so a rule that is not
         on the element does not exist. That is why this file is verbose and why a `class` would
         be decoration rather than styling.
      2. **Tables do the layout.** Outlook renders through Word, which supports neither flexbox
         nor grid. A `role="presentation"` table is the only layout primitive that behaves the
         same in Outlook, Gmail and Apple Mail.
      3. **It is light, while the application is dark.** Not an oversight: a dark HTML email is
         re-tinted unpredictably by client dark-mode heuristics, and these messages carry things —
         a temporary password, a purchase to approve — where "renders correctly everywhere" beats
         "matches the app". The brand still arrives, as the accent on the rule and the button.

    Branding: `brandColor` and `organizationName` are optional context keys with platform
    defaults. The membership messages already pass `organizationName`, so those arrive under the
    trainer's own name; the rest fall back to the platform's. They are not resolved here from `viewer_branding()` on purpose — that function reads
    the *current viewer's* security context, and half of these messages are sent with no viewer at
    all (the approval expiry sweep runs from cron, FR-096) or by somebody other than the recipient
    (a Super Admin creating a trainer). Getting a trainer's colour onto their members' mail means
    the three `*Mailer` services resolving the organization's branding and passing these two keys,
    which is two more entries in a context array rather than a change to this layout.

    Blocks: `email_content` (required), `preheader` (the inbox preview line), `email_title`,
    `email_footer_note` (optional extra small print).
#}
{% set brand = brandColor|default('#006600') %}
{% set orgName = organizationName|default(app_name) %}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>{% block email_title %}{{ orgName }}{% endblock %}</title>
</head>
<body style="margin:0; padding:0; width:100%; background-color:#f3f4f3;">
    {#
        The preheader: the line a client shows in the inbox next to the subject. Without one it
        shows the first words of the body, which for most of these is "Hello,". Hidden in the
        rendered message by zero height and a transparent colour — the combination that works in
        Gmail, Apple Mail and Outlook alike.
    #}
    <div style="display:none; max-height:0; overflow:hidden; mso-hide:all; font-size:1px; line-height:1px; color:#f3f4f3;">
        {% block preheader %}{% endblock %}
    </div>

    <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"
           style="background-color:#f3f4f3; width:100%;">
        <tr>
            <td align="center" style="padding:24px 12px;">

                <table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="600"
                       style="width:600px; max-width:100%; background-color:#ffffff; border:1px solid #e0e3e0; border-radius:12px;">

                    {#
                        The masthead is the organization's name as text, not its logo. A remote
                        image is blocked by default in most clients until the recipient asks for
                        it, so a logo-only header is a blank box on first read — and inline SVG,
                        the other option, is stripped by Gmail entirely.
                    #}
                    <tr>
                        <td style="padding:24px 28px 0 28px;">
                            <p style="margin:0; font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:22px; font-weight:600; color:#1c1f1c;">
                                {{ orgName }}
                            </p>
                        </td>
                    </tr>

                    {# The brand's one appearance as colour: a rule under the masthead. #}
                    <tr>
                        <td style="padding:14px 28px 0 28px;">
                            <div style="height:3px; line-height:3px; font-size:0; background-color:{{ brand }}; border-radius:2px;">&nbsp;</div>
                        </td>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td style="padding:22px 28px 28px 28px; font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:15px; line-height:24px; color:#1c1f1c;">
                            {% block email_content %}{% endblock %}
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                </table>

                <table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="600"
                       style="width:600px; max-width:100%;">
                    <tr>
                        <td style="padding:16px 28px 0 28px; font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:12px; line-height:18px; color:#5e5e5e;">
                            {% block email_footer_note %}{% endblock %}
                            <p style="margin:8px 0 0 0;">
                                Sent by {{ orgName }}. If a link above does not work, copy it into your
                                browser's address bar.
                            </p>
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                </table>

            </td>
        </tr>
    </table>
</body>
</html>
